cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Metodix Library
message: >-
  If you use this library — or a method definition from it — please cite it
  using the metadata below. For a single article, cite the library release and
  name the article by its permanent identifier and version, e.g.
  "Konsensus ja dissensus [03-konsensus-dissensus v1.2], Metodix Library v0.1.0".
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  An open, versioned library of Delphi and futures research method articles,
  written in three registers — for facilitators, for panelists, and for the
  public — in English, Finnish and Swedish. Each release is archived with its own
  DOI, so a study can cite the method definition that was in force when it ran,
  rather than the current one.
authors:
  - name: Metodix Oy
    city: Helsinki
    country: FI
    email: info@metodix.fi
    website: https://www.metodix.eu
repository-code: https://github.com/oraakkeli/metodix-library
url: https://github.com/oraakkeli/metodix-library
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - Delphi method
  - futures research
  - foresight
  - research methodology
  - expert panels
  - consensus and dissensus
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-03
# Concept DOI: always resolves to the most recent release. Cite this when you mean
# "the library". A study cites the version DOI of the tag it ran under instead — see
# `identifiers` below.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21768887
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21768887
    description: Concept DOI — resolves to the latest release
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21768888
    description: Version DOI — Metodix Library v0.1.0
